# ---------------------------- data & models -------------------------------
# Product images and generated catalogues are never committed: the upstream
# dataset declares no licence, and the files are large.
# Regenerate with: python scripts/prepare_sample.py
#
# This is an ALLOW-LIST rather than a list of known directories. Denying
# `data/full/`, `data/raw/` etc. individually meant a later-added `data/eval/`
# was silently trackable - 6,000 images that nearly got committed. Ignoring
# everything under data/ and re-including only what belongs in the repository
# cannot fail that way.
data/*
!data/README.md
!data/sample/
data/sample/*
!data/sample/products.csv
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Downloaded model weights.
# Anchored with a leading slash: a bare `models/` also matched
# backend/app/models/ and silently excluded the entire ORM package.
.cache/
/models/
*.safetensors
*.bin
!**/package-lock.json

# --------------------------- evaluation output ----------------------------
# Reports are regenerated by scripts/evaluate.py and scripts/run_experiments.py.
# The committed report under evaluation/results/ is the one referenced by the
# README; ad-hoc runs land here and stay untracked.
evaluation/results/runs/

